---
import CalculatorLayout from '@/layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro'
import { getToolBySlug, getCategoryBySlug } from '@/data/tools'
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content'
import { TraditionalIRACalculator } from '@/components/calculators/traditional-ira-calculator/index.tsx'

const tool = getToolBySlug('traditional-ira-calculator')!
const category = getCategoryBySlug(tool.category)!
const entry = await getEntry('tools', 'traditional-ira-calculator')
const { data } = entry!
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Traditional IRA Calculator - Tax-Deferred Retirement Savings | FinCalc Pro"
  description={data.description}
  toolName={tool.name}
  category={tool.category}
  categoryName={category.name}
  toolDescription={data.description}
  faqs={data.faqs}
  relatedSlug={tool.slug}
  taxYear="2026"
>
  <div slot="calculator">
    <TraditionalIRACalculator client:load />
  </div>
  <p slot="intro" class="text-muted-foreground mb-8">
    A <strong>Traditional IRA calculator</strong> helps you plan for retirement with the advantage of tax-deferred growth. Contributions may be tax-deductible, reducing your taxable income now, and your investments grow tax-free until withdrawal.
  </p>
  <div slot="how-to-use">
    <p>Enter your current age, current Traditional IRA balance, planned annual contribution, expected annual return, your target retirement age, your current tax bracket, and your expected tax bracket in retirement. The calculator projects your balance at retirement and shows the after-tax value of your withdrawals.</p>
  </div>
  <div slot="formula">
    <p>The accumulation phase uses the standard future value formula:</p>
    <p class="font-mono text-sm bg-muted p-3 rounded">FV = P × (1 + r/n)^(n×t) + PMT × [ ((1 + r/n)^(n×t) − 1) / (r/n) ]</p>
    <p>The after-tax value of withdrawals is shown as: After-tax value = FV × (1 − expected_retirement_tax_rate). This highlights the key trade-off: you get a tax deduction now but pay taxes on withdrawals in retirement at your then-current rate.</p>
  </div>
</CalculatorLayout>
